<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">About Prime Tiles</h2>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    <strong class="font-semibold text-[#111827]">Prime Tiles</strong> sells tiles and finishing materials online, where customers often don't know the exact product name or SKU they're looking for &mdash; just a rough idea of the look, size, or material they want.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-4 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">The challenge</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Traditional keyword search failed customers who couldn't describe what they wanted in the exact terms the catalog used. Searches for things like &ldquo;grey bathroom tiles&rdquo; or &ldquo;outdoor patio stone&rdquo; often returned nothing useful, and customers left without buying.
  </p>
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-6">
    <p class="mb-2 font-medium text-[#111827]">Key pain points:</p>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">
      <li>&bull; Keyword search missed products described in everyday language</li>
      <li>&bull; Customers abandoned searches that returned no results</li>
      <li>&bull; Large catalog made manual browsing impractical</li>
      <li>&bull; Conversion rates lagged behind in-store sales</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-4 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">The solution</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Prime Tiles deployed Zunkiree Search to power an AI-native product search experience. Customers can now describe what they want in natural language and get relevant products instantly, even without knowing exact product names.
  </p>
  <div class="space-y-3">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-100/60 bg-white p-5 shadow-subtle">
      <p class="mb-1 font-medium text-[#111827]">Natural language product search</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-[#6B7280]">Customers search the way they'd describe a product in person &mdash; by look, room, or material &mdash; and get relevant results.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-100/60 bg-white p-5 shadow-subtle">
      <p class="mb-1 font-medium text-[#111827]">Visual and semantic matching</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-[#6B7280]">The system understands product attributes beyond exact keyword matches, surfacing relevant alternatives.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-100/60 bg-white p-5 shadow-subtle">
      <p class="mb-1 font-medium text-[#111827]">Zero-result recovery</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-[#6B7280]">Searches that would have returned nothing now surface the closest relevant matches instead.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-4 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">The results</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
    {% for result in resource.results %}
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#76B900]/20 bg-[#76B900]/[0.06] p-5 text-center">
      <p class="text-[16px] font-medium text-[#111827]">{{ result }}</p>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p class="mt-4 text-[12px] text-navy-400">
    Illustrative results based on a representative engagement; individual outcomes vary and are not guaranteed.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-4 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Why it mattered</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    A bigger keyword dictionary or more synonyms would only have covered more of the phrases Prime Tiles' team could think to anticipate &mdash; it wouldn't have covered the ones they couldn't. The fix wasn't a better list of keywords; it was a search that understands what a customer means, not just the words they happened to type.
  </p>
  <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-[#76B900] pl-4 text-[15px] italic leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">
    &ldquo;We kept adding synonyms to our search index and kept missing the same customers. The problem was never the dictionary.&rdquo;
    <span class="mt-2 block not-italic text-[13px] text-navy-400">&mdash; E-commerce Manager, Prime Tiles</span>
  </blockquote>
</div>

<div class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-100/60 bg-white p-8 shadow-subtle" data-reveal>
  <blockquote class="mb-4 text-[19px] italic leading-relaxed text-[#111827]">
    &ldquo;Customers were leaving because they couldn't find what they wanted in our own search bar. Now they describe the tile they're picturing and actually find it &mdash; our conversion rate doubled almost immediately.&rdquo;
  </blockquote>
  <p class="text-[14px] text-[#6B7280]">
    <strong class="font-semibold text-[#111827]">E-commerce Manager</strong><br>
    Prime Tiles
  </p>
</div>

